{"id": "EUVD-2026-90748", "enisaUuid": "9f98fa27-5deb-377b-90bc-018cc132700d", "description": "ground-station versions before 0.8.0 contain an authentication bypass vulnerability in the setup.restore command that allows unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary SQL during first-run setup mode. Attackers can invoke setup.restore via Socket.IO to plant admin users and forged session tokens, then authenticate as administrator without credentials for complete application takeover.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T10:41:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T13:25:20", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgoudelis/ground-station/security/advisories/GHSA-3mqj-q84c-crjq", "https://github.com/sgoudelis/ground-station/commit/940df2128e57fa779d0ddee2d9726bd829fc61e1", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ground-station-before-0.8.0-authentication-bypass-via-setup-restore"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103244", "GHSA-wwmv-hj9m-4mcc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a65824e8-2358-3ae2-9bb4-272e8d0293bf", "product": {"name": "ground-station", "vendor": {"name": "sgoudelis"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "72b2ddd8-053f-3853-9274-3a8e82afe4c8", "vendor": {"name": "sgoudelis"}}], "isExploited": false}